maria: Opening a small PR to the error-ref for an odd streaming case I ran into — streaming socket resets when the model hits a context limit vs a timeout. PR: https://git.internal/redwood/docs/pull/1421 please eyeball the SDK snippets and the guidance section.
ajay: Nice. Can you outline expected behaviors we want to document? e.g. 1) when to switch to non-streaming fallback, 2) how to trim history vs truncate new tokens, 3) explicit 429 handling.
maria: Proposed text in the PR: prefer incremental prefix trimming (drop oldest assistant/user turns) before lowering max_new_tokens. For streaming: recommend graceful downgrade to non-streaming generation with a resume token in-app.
sam: Add a note that streaming resets can surface as ECONNRESET or a 499-like client-closed in some infra. Also call out case: model returns a short completion and then a 429 on follow-up kv cache fetches — we should show code to parse Retry-After and retry with exponential backoff.
lina: I can add a concrete Node + Python snippet. Quick question: do we want the SDK snippet to use the new .retry() helper or show manual fetch + headers parsing?
ajay: Show both: short example using .retry() for quick adoption, and a manual example for fine-grained control (parsing Retry-After, switching to non-stream).
maria: Draft snippet (inline) ->
```
// pseudo-Node: fallback from streaming to poll-based
const stream = client.responses.stream({model: 'base', input});
try {
  for await (const chunk of stream) process(chunk);
} catch (err) {
  if (err.code === 'CONTEXT_EXHAUSTED' || err.message.includes('socket reset')) {
    // downgrade to non-streaming generation and trim history
    const trimmed = trimHistory(history, {dropTurns: 2});
    const resp = await client.responses.create({model: 'base', input: trimmed, max_new_tokens: 256});
    handle(resp);
  } else if (err.status === 429) {
    const retryAfter = parseInt(err.headers['retry-after'] || '1');
    await sleep(Math.min(30, retryAfter * 2));
    return client.responses.create({model: 'base', input, retry: {retries: 3}});
  }
  throw err;
}
```
maria: I'll put that in the PR under "streaming-interrupts" section with a short UX note.
lina: I'll add the Python equivalent and a short test prompt that reproduces context exhaustion in local harness so docs CI can smoke it.
sam: Also add a small paragraph about what to log: final token counts, last-turn ids, and any Retry-After header values. That helps support triage.
